Package: bushfireheat
Title: Explore Fire-Season Heat in South-Eastern Australia
Version: 0.0.0.9000
Authors@R: 
    person("Hanwen", "Liu", , "hliu0223@student.monash.edu", role = c("aut", "cre"))
Description: Daily maximum temperature and rainfall from the ERA5
    reanalysis for eight towns in south-eastern Australia affected by the
    2019/20 Black Summer fires. Functions count hot days in each September
    to February fire season, compare a recent period with a mid-century
    baseline and plot the result, and a Shiny app lets users explore how
    often extreme fire-season heat now occurs and how sensitive that
    change is to the temperature threshold.
